# "Johan can't attack" is an ability Johan gains (CR 113.1a), but "attacking doesn't cause creatures you control to tap" is a
# rule of the game, no ability of anything (CR 611.2c). Bot1 says yes on turn 3, then turns its own Johan into a Frog that
# has lost all its abilities (Turn to Frog, CR 613.1f): Johan may attack again, the rule still holds, and Johan is itself an
# untapped creature Bot1 controls, so it attacks without becoming tapped (CR 508.1f) and deals 1 damage as a 1/1.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Johan
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Turn to Frog
Plains x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Johan.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Turn to Frog.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Johan)
[T3 Bot1.Attackers]
Bot1.Attack(Johan > Bot2)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Johan.Tapped = false
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Johan.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Johan.Power = 1
Bot2.Life = 19
